[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-9f1e2a51-8de3-4d48-b8ee-41075e3873d9\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"9f1e2a51-8de3-4d48-b8ee-41075e3873d9\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>TheBotCompany: Self-Organizing Multi-agent Systems for Continuous Software Development</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Large language model (LLM)-based multi-agent systems have shown promise in automating software development tasks. However, most vibe-coding systems focus on completing small tasks and incremental code changes, leaving persistent, continuous software development largely unexplored. We present TheBotCompany, an open-source orchestration framework for continuous multi-agent software development. TheBotCompany introduces three key innovations: (1) a three-phase state machine (Strategy to Execution to Verification) for milestone-driven development, (2) self-organizing agent teams where manager agents dynamically hire, assign, and retire worker agents based on project needs, and (3) asynchronous human oversight. We evaluate TheBotCompany on real-world software projects over multiple days of continuous development, measuring team adaptation patterns, milestone completion rates, cost efficiency, and code quality. Our results demonstrate that the self-organizing approach enables effective long-term software development with measurable progress, while the verification phase catches defects that would otherwise persist.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3834358\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> DOI</a><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.25928\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> Pre-print</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/wenhanlyu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Wenhan Lyu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">William &amp; Mary</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/yuexiao\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yue Xiao<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">William &amp; Mary</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/yixuanzhang1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yixuan Zhang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">William &amp; Mary</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/yifansun1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yifan Sun<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">William &amp; Mary</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/28/TheBotCompany-Self-Organizing-Multi-agent-Systems-for-Continuous-Software-Developmen\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-9f1e2a51-8de3-4d48-b8ee-41075e3873d9').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
